Under the FSS Licensing & Registration Regulations 2011, manufacturers and importers must establish and maintain a documented system for handling product returns. This system must:

* Clearly define the procedures for receiving, inspecting, and evaluating returned items;
* Identify the circumstances under which a return is required (e.g., safety defects, non‑conformity to approved specifications, or consumer complaints);
* Specify the time frames within which returns must be processed and reported to the Food Safety Authority of Ireland (FSAI);
* Ensure that returned products are either safely destroyed, re‑conditioned, or returned to the supplier in accordance with the relevant safety and quality standards;
* Keep accurate records of all returns, including product details, reasons for return, actions taken, and any corrective measures implemented;
* Make these records available for inspection by the FSAI upon request.

Failure to implement such a returns management system or to comply with the reporting and record‑keeping obligations constitutes a breach of the 2011 Regulations.
